Mermaid renders plain text into diagrams. This wiki uses [[mermaid-tw5|$:/plugins/orange/mermaid-tw5]], a plugin built on [[Mermaid 11.14.0|https://mermaid.js.org]]. Twenty-six diagram types are available.

---

!! Flows and Processes

|!Diagram|!Best for|
|[[Flowchart]]|Algorithms, workflows, decision trees|
|[[Sequence Diagram]]|API interactions, protocol flows, actor communication|
|[[User Journey]]|UX flows, customer experience mapping|

!! Data and Metrics

|!Diagram|!Best for|
|[[Pie Chart]]|Proportional data at a glance|
|[[XY Chart]]|Bar and line charts with numeric axes|
|[[Quadrant Chart]]|2×2 prioritization and positioning matrices|
|[[Sankey Diagram]]|Flow and allocation — where things come from and go|
|[[Radar Chart]]|Multi-axis skill or attribute comparison|
|[[Treemap]]|Hierarchical part-to-whole proportions|

!! Architecture and Systems

|!Diagram|!Best for|
|[[C4 Diagram]]|System context, containers, components (C4 model)|
|[[Architecture Diagram]]|Cloud / service topology and infrastructure|
|[[Block Diagram]]|Component-level architecture with explicit layout|
|[[Packet Diagram]]|Network protocols, binary frame formats|
|[[Wardley Map]]|Strategic positioning of components along an evolution axis|

!! Software and Data Modeling

|!Diagram|!Best for|
|[[Class Diagram]]|OOP class relationships and data models|
|[[Entity Relationship]]|Database schema, entity relationships|
|[[State Diagram]]|State machines, lifecycle flows|
|[[Git Graph]]|Git branching and merge history|

!! Planning and Management

|!Diagram|!Best for|
|[[Gantt]]|Project scheduling, task dependencies|
|[[Kanban Board]]|Task workflow, sprint boards|
|[[Timeline]]|Historical events, milestones, version history|
|[[Requirement Diagram]]|Systems engineering requirements traceability|

!! Exploration and Thinking

|!Diagram|!Best for|
|[[Mindmap]]|Brainstorming, topic maps, hierarchical thinking|
|[[Venn Diagram]]|Set relationships and overlapping categories|
|[[Ishikawa Diagram]]|Root-cause analysis (fishbone diagrams)|
|[[Tree View]]|File trees, org charts, nested hierarchies|

